{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20","id":1433402,"title":"Crossover Changeling The Dreaming (C20) and Vampire The Masquerade (V20)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-25T09:09:50-08:00","id":1433402,"title":"Crossover Changeling The Dreaming (C20) and Vampire The Masquerade (V20)","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I would love to narrate a Crossover between Vampires and Changelings but I have no idea how to start. Could anyone give me an idea about why vampires ally with Changelings? Please <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (Just a few vampires, it doesn't have to be an entire city or cult.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T09:36:25-08:00","id":1433405,"title":"","content":"Some may do so in return for the sparkly special blood of the Changeling - especially the Malkavians and Tremer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T09:54:41-08:00","id":1433408,"title":"","content":"The bigger question I think that needs answering is why would Changeling go any where near the banality source that is a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T10:24:58-08:00","id":1433410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433408#post1433408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger question I think that needs answering is why would Changeling go any where near the banality source that is a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe that not every vampire has a lot of banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:11:35-08:00","id":1433417,"title":"","content":"Yeah I\u2019m also of the opinion that most (young) vampires would be better sources of Nightmare Glamour then of Banality, although their banal factor increases with age. That idea alone though does make them better allies for Unseelie and Thallain but not as a hard rule.<br /> <br /> As with anything this depends on specific circumstances. What kind of Changelings you have and what the interests of the chronicle are, but generally speaking, here are some ideas:<br /> <br /> \u2022Clan Malkavian has an old standing idea they have a relationship swift Changelings and while this can be handled irresponsibly I think one could handle the concept of the Malkavians being disparate from reality allowing them greater comprehension of Changelings and the Dreaming well.<br /> <br /> \u2022Clans like the Brujah and Toreador are passionate and could be great reservoirs or glamour if either party took interest in the works of the other<br /> <br /> \u2022Vampires are territorial so a motley could end up in a working relationship with the vampire whose domain they frequent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T18:09:09-08:00","id":1433439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433408#post1433408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bigger question I think that needs answering is why would Changeling go any where near the banality source that is a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solid point, only a small number of Vampires are low banality. Most of those are either A) in Golconda or nearly there, or B) Malkavians deeply disconnected from the world around them. Thus either way over or under powered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T07:19:02-08:00","id":1433500,"title":"","content":"Frankly I never understood the &quot;vampires are banal&quot; stuff being based on humanity. Humanity is a <b>morality path </b>and if you're telling me glamour and banality have anything to do with morality, then the sidhe should no exist, because they are immoral authoritharians.<br /> <br /> Now, I could understand saying a vampire is banal because he is neck deep in the jyhad, to the point he thinks of everything as chess pieces and see judges everything just by its usefulness to him. But tying it to humanity, I see no sense in this. Thallain are more monstrous than most vampires and they are not banal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T18:04:34-08:00","id":1433562,"title":"","content":"I thought of a plot hook where someone or something has been abducting Changlings to sell their blood to vampires as a drug, which would lead to the local Camarilla and Changling freehold to have a temporary truce to investigate. The Camarilla doesn\u2019t like the fact of possible Sabbat aligned operations causing Vampires to twitch their balls and do random stupid shit, and the Changlings don\u2019t like being abducted and being used as juice bags","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T18:57:23-08:00","id":1433568,"title":"","content":"My changeling character (a Swan Maiden) and her friend (a satyr who loves biochemistry) developed a potion using both Glamour and blood magic that would allow Kindred to enjoy sex again, but our ST ruled that most vampires\u2019 Banality is so high it counteracts the Glamour in the potion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T04:14:13-08:00","id":1433599,"title":"","content":"To make it simple, i would not include or lean heavily into the &quot;vampires are banality&quot;-trope unless you want to have this as a center piece of your story and if you want the Changelings to interact with the vampires in a friendly manner.<br /> <br /> You can easily portray the vampires as dream fuel for nightmares, dreams of desire, lust, hunger and power. But also as inherintl<br /> <br /> One cornerstone is - Both love deals - were as - vampires normally only honour deals trough I.O.U (and actually only among themselvers) and changelings have pledges/oaths.<br /> -- But in my headcannon - changelings/fae are just not worth the trouble, downright dangerous or to chaotic when you have a Masquerade to uphold - also making deals with them is like making deals with the devil. Drinking changeling blood is dangerously trippy - and many vampires tell the story of the one who drank a fae and then mistook the day for the night and then burned to a crisp in the sun, while plucking dasies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T15:30:57-08:00","id":1433659,"title":"","content":"A local vampire and changeling are in love. Borrow heavily from Romeo &amp; Juliet, Tristan &amp; Iseult, Hero &amp; Leander, Wuthering Heights, Othello, As You Like It, and The Phantom of the Opera as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T18:25:06-08:00","id":1433673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433659#post1433659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A local vampire and changeling are in love. Borrow heavily from Romeo &amp; Juliet, Tristan &amp; Iseult, Hero &amp; Leander, Wuthering Heights, Othello, As You Like It, and The Phantom of the Opera as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do this, the Changeling is the spooky one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T18:41:17-08:00","id":1433674,"title":"","content":"You could always go the Kiasyd route. Under some rulings, they are already part fae and partly effected by Glamour. Plus, they are now masters at mixing magical effects into blood, something that goes hand in hand with Changelings. If a Changeling spots a Kiasyd one night, this could start a whole investigation into who and what it actually is. Could also be beneficial, as Kiasyd are also information brokers. A trade could be made that could lead to further investigations. There are also the Maegar, fae that got embraced to become vampires. Very rare, even compared to other Kindred. Also pathetic. Even a mere trace of one being near by could be the start of a chase to find the truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T18:49:03-08:00","id":1433675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433673#post1433673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you do this, the Changeling is the spooky one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which game you are running, I think. If Masquerade and one of the PCs or an important NPC is infatuated with the Queen of Air and Darkness, Slenderman, or a nine-tailed fox spirit, then most definitely. But if Changeling, the the vampire might be the full blown Dark and Brooding Byronic Phantom Lover type. You could really play it multiple ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T01:35:36-08:00","id":1433689,"title":"","content":"My swan maiden loves the idea of a dark and brooding Byronic vampire lover \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T06:29:55-08:00","id":1433700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433689#post1433689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My swan maiden loves the idea of a dark and brooding Byronic vampire lover \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>There probably needs to be fan art for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T18:35:49-08:00","id":1433967,"title":"","content":"c20 does not promote Vampires as having pariticularly high banality if one looks at the various stated out Prodigals,actin general prodigals even at their worst tend to be less banal than your average mortal.... this probably matches up with a certain amount of common sense I mean how can someone who lives and breaths magic be particular banal?<br /> <br /> On the other hand it broadly does push the idea that it is a commonly held belief among changelings that Vampire are banality incarnate and that only unseelie rebels really see it differently. Then I thought about how Vampire generally works and came to an epiphany.<br /> <br /> Being a Vampire is not a banal act. But things that tend to push someone to high banality is a survival strategy for the long term vampire. The long term survival strategies of changelings vs Vampire are intrinsically at odds and can create a very interesting star crossed lovers trope.<br /> <br /> So how does being Banal help your vampire survive... Well.. Humanity/Roads/Paths of Enlightenment. Quite simply the drive to become less engaged to day to day &quot;Adventuring&quot; is sort of built into the Kindred condition. A static controlled routine is generally how one engages in a night to night life for the long term for a vampire no matter their path. Its why they work through ghouls, and neonates and pawns because the less they engage in the less they have to risk having their world view questioned and thus keep the beast at bay. This is why most kindred die young. They never get out of this pawn stage and cannot control their routine.. the perfect allies and friends for your average changeling.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately of course as they move higher up in the board they find the routine a strong drive and the changeling of course needs.. chaos they need novelty they need to adventure. Their friendships and loves become poisons.... but such is the way of love.. just ask a Varich.<br /> <br /> Now i am sure many of you will point out to Paths like Metamorphosis for things that promote chaos and change... but it doesn't. It promotes a very regimented and controlled focus you in control. It even goes so far as to remove you from kindred society at its highest ends. Yes becoming a hermit temple made of flesh is creepy body horror... its also you banal as fuck after a couple of years.<br /> <br /> Conversely those particularly low and in unstable states on their path might gain a new found understanding by engaging with the changeling... growing ot they point of exemplarship.. or climbing up from the brink of wassail by the grace of glamour.. that they eventually turn against.. such is the tragedy of Kindred existance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-30-2021, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T08:10:01-08:00","id":1434017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433967#post1433967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c20 does not promote Vampires as having pariticularly high banality if one looks at the various stated out Prodigals,actin general prodigals even at their worst tend to be less banal than your average mortal.... this probably matches up with a certain amount of common sense I mean how can someone who lives and breaths magic be particular banal?<br /> <br /> On the other hand it broadly does push the idea that it is a commonly held belief among changelings that Vampire are banality incarnate and that only unseelie rebels really see it differently. Then I thought about how Vampire generally works and came to an epiphany.<br /> <br /> Being a Vampire is not a banal act. But things that tend to push someone to high banality is a survival strategy for the long term vampire. The long term survival strategies of changelings vs Vampire are intrinsically at odds and can create a very interesting star crossed lovers trope.<br /> <br /> So how does being Banal help your vampire survive... Well.. Humanity/Roads/Paths of Enlightenment. Quite simply the drive to become less engaged to day to day &amp;quot;Adventuring&amp;quot; is sort of built into the Kindred condition. A static controlled routine is generally how one engages in a night to night life for the long term for a vampire no matter their path. Its why they work through ghouls, and neonates and pawns because the less they engage in the less they have to risk having their world view questioned and thus keep the beast at bay. This is why most kindred die young. They never get out of this pawn stage and cannot control their routine.. the perfect allies and friends for your average changeling.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately of course as they move higher up in the board they find the routine a strong drive and the changeling of course needs.. chaos they need novelty they need to adventure. Their friendships and loves become poisons.... but such is the way of love.. just ask a Varich.<br /> <br /> Now i am sure many of you will point out to Paths like Metamorphosis for things that promote chaos and change... but it doesn't. It promotes a very regimented and controlled focus you in control. It even goes so far as to remove you from kindred society at its highest ends. Yes becoming a hermit temple made of flesh is creepy body horror... its also you banal as fuck after a couple of years.<br /> <br /> Conversely those particularly low and in unstable states on their path might gain a new found understanding by engaging with the changeling... growing ot they point of exemplarship.. or climbing up from the brink of wassail by the grace of glamour.. that they eventually turn against.. such is the tragedy of Kindred existance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating! I totally agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T16:39:29-08:00","id":1434199,"title":"","content":"Of course the changeling has alot to offer to a vampire who wants out... Spring might give them a taste of rebirth for a day.. naming might undo the whole curse of caine... Such things are quite dangerous for the static of kindred society... causing all sorts of chaos for those carefully crafted elders...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T20:27:25-08:00","id":1434219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433500#post1433500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly I never understood the &quot;vampires are banal&quot; stuff being based on humanity. Humanity is a <b>morality path </b>and if you're telling me glamour and banality have anything to do with morality, then the sidhe should no exist, because they are immoral authoritharians.<br /> <br /> Now, I could understand saying a vampire is banal because he is neck deep in the jyhad, to the point he thinks of everything as chess pieces and see judges everything just by its usefulness to him. But tying it to humanity, I see no sense in this. Thallain are more monstrous than most vampires and they are not banal.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've always equated the High Banality bit about Vampires with their age, and not their curse or humanity.<br /> After all, as they become older they tend to become more set in their ways. Elder vampires are unable to adapt to newer technologies or political outlooks, not because they <b>can't </b>(after all they usually have rather high mental attributes) but rather because they don't care to. They tend to believe their ways are better. Why use Facetime when a phonecall is just as good? or when a written letter would be far more striking and elegant? <br /> Imagine my elder aunt, who refuses to have WiFi installed at her house, even if it is included in her phone-company bill already, just because she &quot;doesn't think it is necesary&quot; (yes... even through the pandemic). Now multiply imagine she were a vampire 200 years older than she is... Obviously she would insist on outdated politics and anachronistic technologies, without seeing the merits of change and newness.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the changelings' efforts to protect their freehold against gentrification has not gone unnoticed by the local kindred. Perhaps he wants to exploit the &quot;artsy&quot;, &quot;old world&quot; feel of the community for her own businesses success...<br /> Or for a darker story, perhaps the local Unseelie noble has struck some oaths with the local Prince. They help the vampires find Herd, and in exchange they get to feed on their mounting terror as they are bled dry...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T20:48:37-08:00","id":1434220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luisarmander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1434219#post1434219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I've always equated the High Banality bit about Vampires with their age, and not their curse or humanity.<br /> After all, as they become older they tend to become more set in their ways. Elder vampires are unable to adapt to newer technologies or political outlooks, not because they <b>can't </b>(after all they usually have rather high mental attributes) but rather because they don't care to. They tend to believe their ways are better. Why use Facetime when a phonecall is just as good? or when a written letter would be far more striking and elegant?<br /> Imagine my elder aunt, who refuses to have WiFi installed at her house, even if it is included in her phone-company bill already, just because she &quot;doesn't think it is necesary&quot; (yes... even through the pandemic). Now multiply imagine she were a vampire 200 years older than she is... Obviously she would insist on outdated politics and anachronistic technologies, without seeing the merits of change and newness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its more to it than that. Especially given how Facebook has been taken up by the elderly. I think kindred condition DOES support banality as a long term survival strategy. If you've ever seen the Movie He Never Died. is perhaps the best example of what its like to be an Elder Kindred. The Main character has a strictly regimented life, and then plot happens and he starts falling off the wagon and you can see him taking basically degeneration checks.. decades of careful work to keep the beast at bay unravels over a weekend.<br /> <br /> The more you engage in actions outside your control the more you engage in potential sins. And it so much easier to lose than it is to gain. Its so easy to wassail. I mean your 200 year ancilla probably saw half their neonate cotorie wassail by then.. by the time they are an elder they might be the only one left. They know how easy it is.. so they work to control everything... they don't even work to destroy their enemies anymore just to thwart their plans because having an enemy is stability.<br /> <br /> Its why for all the power of Elders its the Young vampires that seem to change the world. Just like the youngest changelings can shrug off banality until they've hit a point where they need to pay attention to glamour vampires run in reverse.. they shrug off chaos as they start with high humanity.. or they have the emotional strength to climb up the ladder quickly.... but then they need stasis they need banality as a life preserver against the Beast.<br /> <br /> Its sad and tragic, especially as whole clans were dedicated to art.<br /> <br /> Luckily you can do the right thing as you know recinarnation is real!<br /> <br /> (This is why Kindred are scared the shit of fairies..)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T16:17:25-08:00","id":1469211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1433967#post1433967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">c20 does not promote Vampires as having pariticularly high banality</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does.<br /> pg 268, where Angels fear to Tread.<br /> <br /> Elysium is a Banal structure. The Camarilla is a banal organisation it exists <b>only</b> for the purposes of the Elders, operates in a ruthlessly enforced top down heirarchy. Every non camarilla vampire is wrong, or worse yet evil. There is no room for discussion about the laws. They measure their banality in years and Status. The more Status you have, the more you have bought into the structure.<br /> <br /> Courts themselves are just an attempt to shove off the infinite boredom of eternity. Everything about Elysium is banal.<br /> <br /> Banality is contagious. The more courts you go to the higher your banality creeps. &quot;Mortals who regularly spend time in a Banal structure with a higher banality than their own slowly gain Banality until they reach equilibrium with that Structure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampires are frozen in time at their Embrace, literally. They are a representation of stasis and that is Banal.<br /> <br /> They accrue Banality and have no means to slough it off. They can't be brought on Quests, they can't gain Glamour. Inevitability itself gives them a Banal tinge.<br /> <br /> Malkavians are not exempted from this in C20. Only in C2. And Malkavians would represent the further threat of Bedlam. Which is equally as contagious as Banal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13114-cuannan","name":"CuAnnan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T00:16:39-08:00","id":1469236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CuAnnan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1469211#post1469211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes it does.<br /> pg 268, where Angels fear to Tread.</div> </div> </div> </div>As interesting as your assertions are, and possibly true, they are not in the book. That was the point.<br /> <br /> <b>You</b> are saying Elysium is a banal structure, and you are making all those assertions. The book isn't. What the book actually have are three statblocks, a Neonate with Banality 3, Ancilla with Banality 6 and Elder with Banality 8. And no assertion about their structures, organizations or anything.<br /> <br /> Other than that, some of your conclusions are solid and sound, other not so much. A place's Banality have nothing to do with the organizations it serves or their ideals, so the Camarilla has zero to do with it. It depends on the people who frequent it, and Elysium may be frequented by a varied bunch and host a kind of intrigue-filled party that would make many a Sidhe envious. This can be interpreted as Glamour, so much so that C20 <b><i>explicitly</i></b> says that unseelie Changelings frequently do precisely this.<br /> <br /> Fairies used to be just as much frozen in time, and indeed a lot of their political expectations are quite frozen in time. This <b>is not</b> equal to banality.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the actual book says they can't slough off Banality in the same way a mortal does, or that they acquire Banality easier than a mortal, nothing says that stasis or inevitability bring them Banality, nothing at all says you can't bring them on Quests.<br /> <br /> The conclusions presented may serve you well in your chronicles and are interesting for some games. They make some sense if taken from certain PoV. They are sound, relevant, <b>but not official truths</b> <i>or </i><b>unavoidable conclusions</b>. They're just your take on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T13:42:33-08:00","id":1469269,"title":"","content":"Pg 142 tal mahe Re &quot;Also, any fae in the Underworld or in the presence of Cainites loses one Glamour per day atop of Glamour spent normally. A fae cannot regain Glamour as long as she remains in the presence of vampires and should she fall to 0 Glamour,s he becomes a Catatonic husk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ctd pg 268 &quot;Organizations dedicated to promulgation of one point of view above all others are a common cause of such structures&quot;<br /> <br /> You are welcome to disregard printed mechanics you don't agree with. The Golden Rule and all that.<br /> But vampires as printed are a permanent, existential, neccessary threat to Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13114-cuannan","name":"CuAnnan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T04:21:29-08:00","id":1469304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CuAnnan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1469269#post1469269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pg 142 tal mahe Re &quot;Also, any fae in the Underworld or in the presence of Cainites loses one Glamour per day atop of Glamour spent normally. A fae cannot regain Glamour as long as she remains in the presence of vampires and should she fall to 0 Glamour,s he becomes a Catatonic husk.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, that's a decent source. I do challenge its canon for C20 since it's not a Changeling book, it's a rule for Changelings in a Vampire supplement, so it's arguably official in a Vampire, but it stands that <b>C20 didn't promote it</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CuAnnan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1469269#post1469269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ctd pg 268 &quot;Organizations dedicated to promulgation of one point of view above all others are a common cause of such structures&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still pretty much your reading and not what the text say. There's a huge difference between &quot;this kind of organization is a common cause of high Banality structures&quot; and &quot;this specific organization is the ultimate representation of Banality and always causes their social clubs to be high Banality.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bearing in mind that A) this is a pretty shallow view of the Camarilla to say it is dedicated to the promulgation of one PoV above all others. How do you even define that? Are you sure your definition is objectively true and not your opinion? And B) the Elysium isn't the main Camarilla organizational building <i>par excellence</i>, it is just their social club. Their main organizational institutions are the offices of Prince and, arguably, Primigen, so the building most likely to be affected would be their respective offices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T07:59:44-08:00","id":1469918,"title":"","content":"As a general rule at my games, I treat the Banality of NPC Vampires as more like that of C20 Dauntain. Rather than a deadening of wonder in the vampire itself, but an aura of twisted Glamour that spawns the nastiest sorts of Nightmares. Similarly, their feeding is a type of Ravaging.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Vampires Clans, Banality and troupe play, I treat starting Banality for Vampires as that of Human PC's, starting at Banality 4. Vampires of the Malkavian and Kiasyd clans begin with a Banality of 3, due to their particularly fae natures and Disciplines.<br /> <br /> In my own games, the Nosferatu often have an understanding with local fae, particularly with the Sluagh and Nockers, but other kiths as well. The Nosferatu often live deep underground, and have little to do with Vampire culture, and so aren't nearly as Banal as those who play politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 12-08-2021, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T11:46:19-08:00","id":1470058,"title":"","content":"I think in general vampires should be highly Banal, but exceptions exist. There are any number of reasons why certain individual vampires should be less Banal. I'd usually make these younger vampire or vampires with higher Humanity, but I could come up with scenarios of older and more monstrous vampires being less Banal. There's lot of potentially interesting stories or scenarios where you'd want vampires and fairies interacting so why hamper yourself with an overly strict rule? &quot;Always&quot; and &quot;never&quot; <i>tend</i> to be bad rules. The importance is to rely less on game mechanics, and think of character reasons why this particular vampire is less Banal while still keeping vampires in general Banal.<br /> <br /> I am reluctant to simply make Malkavians <i>in general</i> less Banal though. That is an artifact of the early game when it was assumed that Malkavians had greater knowledge of &quot;true&quot; reality. That was paired with their Derangement, but the underlying assumption of the game was the Malkavians &quot;knew&quot; things other vampires didn't. I question whether that was actually the case. First, very few canonical NPCs were actually depicted like that. Second, while that was something an ST could objectively make true for an NPC, it was always much harder to do that for PCs because you couldn't control what a PC Malkavian did, nor did you want to give preference to one PC over the others. At best, it was simply a pretext an ST could use to provide additional knowledge to a PC that the ST wanted them to have, but an ST could also figure out ways to provide that same knowledge in other ways to other PCs. Third, once the game began to provide actual mechanics to some of these things for Malkavians, it opened up the rift between those Malkavians who might know some things (because they had that on their character sheet) and those Malkavians who wouldn't (because it wasn't on their character sheet). Fourth, not all Malkavian concepts and Derangements lead themselves to the idea that <i>this</i> Malkavian may understand &quot;true reality&quot; better as the game began encouraging more Hannibal Lecter types versus the more whimsical or delusional types. One can argue a Malkavian who is schizophrenic might actually sometimes experience the Umbra or the Dreaming (that giant pink bunny named Harvey that he talks to might be a Pooka or a Chimera), but a Malkavian who is simply a sociopath or have depression shouldn't. So for me, having slightly more Malkavians be less Banal on average that other vampires is better than a strict rule that says all Malkavians are less Banal.<br /> <br /> The other guidance I would use is that not all Banality is the same. The Banality of a dour, strict, and unimaginative human working at the DMV should not be the same as the Banality of an elder vampire, even if that vampire is highly Banal. Mechanically it may play out the same, but how it is presented should be different. The first person is just an unimaginative killjoy that takes the fun out of life with their presence. The second is a force of entropy and death into this world that erodes the life and hope of people and animals it encounters. It reduces humanity to simply being a source of blood to keep itself alive, or being slaves to its desires instead of guardians of their own hopes and dreams. The two beings' Banality should be roleplayed very differently. Therefore when you do encounter a vampire that is somehow less Banal, it provides an appropriate juxtaposition to the vampires in general, and gives a hint on what the future may hold for that character (becoming more Banal as the years takes it tolls, it loses Humanity, kills more people, enslaves people through the Blood Bond, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T18:07:34-08:00","id":1470319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1433402-crossover-changeling-the-dreaming-c20-and-vampire-the-masquerade-v20?p=1470058#post1470058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second is a force of entropy and death into this world that erodes the life and hope of people and animals it encounters. It reduces humanity to simply being a source of blood to keep itself alive, or being slaves to its desires instead of guardians of their own hopes and dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do like your take in general, I'm personally drifting far from the idea of elders as Banal because there's another aspect to the fae that the game have some problem delivering, but needs consideration: a Dream can be a <b>Nightmare</b>.<br /> <br /> For me, today, nightmares are still Glamour. The things that inspire people to tell stories and imagine a terrible world outside is Glamour even if those people decide to stay in home because of their fear. Their hopes may be weaker, but their imagination is on fire.<br /> <br /> The problem here is that, while partially recognizing Changelings linked to nightmares, the game also had always a tendency to side with fantasy-like dreams instead of horror-like ones, and to use the notion of a <i>Greater Nightmare</i> to forge links to other splats' apocalyptic prophecies. It kind of felt right to the authors that Changeling should have an End Prophecy and Evil Enemies of the likes that Vampire and, above all, Werewolf have.<br /> <br /> But for me the right place for nightmare is in the Courts. The Unseelie of rl legend and game lore is the Court of Nightmare. Sluagh are the <i>things that scuttle in the dark places</i>, and Red Caps can literally eat you so easily that snatching a piece of you is a combat maneuver for them.<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't have a dark counterpart because it embraces the darkness in a way no other splat does. Their society thoroughly recognizes villains and predators as members along with heroes and saviors.<br /> <br /> And Vampires... well, they do form the most popular game line, that's at least how much they fire up people's imagination naturally. Why shouldn't the Unseelie theory that their Banality is actually Dark Glamour be true?<br /> <br /> Now, this is just me. Individual tendencies should play the bigger role in any case, and the reading that the undead state naturally brings Banality about is just as valid. But I think the way it was done pays too much heed to Werewolf and little to actual Changeling themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T11:05:17-08:00","id":1470357,"title":"","content":"I certainly believe that some elders are not considered Banal (or even as a source of Glamour). I think there is relatively very few of them though. The real issue is whether they legitimately act as sources of wonder and imagination (and be so ongoing, not an infrequent or inadvertent source by random chance). A monstrous elder who is on the Path of Night is much more likely to serve as one given that they believe vampires serve a higher purpose and seek to fulfill it. Their actions are more likely to be designed to keep mortals aware and in fear so they will acknowledge the great moral powers of the universe. Most elders though simply have more Banal ends - to survive and slake their Hunger. Of course, we're not limited to vampires on the Path of Night. We can come up with lots of theoretical examples (and also have vampires that theoretically should not be Banal, but are in practice).<br /> <br /> People like to be scared - but only in safe situations where they aren't actually in danger of being harmed. If they actually feel under threat, people tend to shut down their minds and concentrate merely on survival and afterwards don't view their past experience positively. It's traumatic, not a source of wonder. Experiences with vampires tend to grind people down which is a very Banal thing. So while I can see certain circumstances where people might be left with a sense of wonder upon interacting with vampires, I think it's very limited. <br /> <br /> It would be much more common for someone to temporarily be curious about the world of vampires before they learn the sudden and real (Banal) truth about it - they're just a meal or a useful slave. The false glamour isn't real. It's the difference between the romanticized version of the mob in the Godfather versus the more realistic depiction in Scorsese movies. Simply because it's false, doesn't mean it can't generate &quot;real&quot; Glamour per the Changeling mechanic. But it has less to do with understanding reality (which is Banal) than the person being so foolish they don't realize the situation they are in. In that case, is it the vampires not being Banal, or is it that their victims are actually the ones not being so? (We can apply it to many other things that are generally thought to be terrible, but some people find adventurous or have fantasies that incorporate only some of the reality while ignoring everything else. War is an obvious one.) There's obviously some room for discussion when it comes to the game mechanics. I believe in general, vampire Banality is high and probably increases over time. But there are exceptions, and a very rare few vampires might actually be sources of actual &quot;Dark Glamour&quot;. As long as the ST really sold it to me that this vampire or this particular encounter isn't Banal, I'd be fine with it. But I don't think it's the default.<br /> <br /> So if I was STing Changeling, and had to make a general rule, I might say &quot;hey, in any situation concerning vampires, it's 90% Banal, but 10% of it is not&quot;. (More likely it's less than that for me.) But different STs would assign different percentages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T17:42:17-08:00","id":1470399,"title":"","content":"The idea that vampires are INTRINSICALLY banal is a holdover from 2nd Edition that is largely absent from 20th Anniversary Rules As Written. The entire parameters surrounding Banality have changed because it is now, largely, unique to the individual. What one Changeling finds Banal another would find Glamorous. Point blank-- vampires are a source of inspiration. Vampires have inspired countless books, movies, paintings, plays, and other works of art. You can use this to explore a Kithain's interest in vampires, particularly any kind of tragic/romantic kind of Cainite (it feels like every coterie has a Toreador or Malkavian these days). Conversely, vampires are also a huge source of fear-- fear can also be extremely Glamorous. Nightmares and the stories of monsters are not intrinsically Banal, so that's another angle you can pursue depending on what vampires are taking the spotlight in your story. A third example-- Gangrel and Pooka. Some vampires, and some faeries, are more connected to the natural world. Plenty of cultures around the world (the Russian vedma comes to mind) blend a vampiric entity with an animal shapeshifter enchantress. <br /> <br /> My impulse thoughts around this issue-- Thinbloods and Kithain would make an interesting story. Thinbloods experimenting with Alchemy meeting a Nocker, wild experiments commence? Sounds Glamorous to me. In general, younger vampires (which, to be fair, recent editions of VTM encourage younger vampires be the stars!) would probably be better companions to the Kithain. Both Masquerade and Dreaming have classicist struggles as a central theme (Elders vs Neonates, Nobles vs Commoners) and that would be interesting to explore. <br /> <br /> I would encourage you not to be discouraged about vampires being intrinsically Banal. The entire point of Dreaming is that the potential for stories are limitless. Personally I think there are some very interesting stories to be told about these two creatures finding themselves at a crossroads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}